1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,099
One day, this city had 20,000 residents.

2
00:00:03,099 --> 00:00:04,854
The next day, it had zero.

3
00:00:04,854 --> 00:00:05,326
No war.

4
00:00:05,326 --> 00:00:06,676
No natural disaster.

5
00:00:06,676 --> 00:00:07,756
Just... silence.

6
00:00:07,756 --> 00:00:10,725
And to this day, nobody fully agrees on why.

7
00:00:11,325 --> 00:00:13,522
This wasn't some forgotten village.

8
00:00:13,522 --> 00:00:18,669
It was a thriving industrial city, with schools, hospitals, and a growing economy.

9
00:00:18,669 --> 00:00:21,180
Families had lived here for generations.

10
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:25,700
Nobody had any reason to believe it would soon be erased from every map.

11
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,239
Looking back, there were signs.

12
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:37,623
Strange reports started months before the evacuation: underground tremors, unexplained gas leaks, and official records that mysteriously went missing.

13
00:00:37,623 --> 00:00:40,438
But local authorities dismissed it as rumors.

14
00:00:41,038 --> 00:00:45,556
Then, within 48 hours, the entire government ordered a full evacuation.

15
00:00:45,556 --> 00:00:48,865
Residents were told they could return within a week.

16
00:00:48,865 --> 00:00:50,711
That week turned into months.

17
00:00:50,711 --> 00:00:51,411
Then years.

18
00:00:51,411 --> 00:00:52,302
Then... never.

19
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:55,483
Today, the city still technically exists on paper.

20
00:00:55,483 --> 00:01:02,038
But if you visit, you'll find nothing but empty streets and buildings slowly being reclaimed by nature.

21
00:01:02,638 --> 00:01:10,616
The official explanation blames a coal mine fire burning underground, one that's technically still burning today, decades later.

22
00:01:10,616 --> 00:01:18,968
But residents who lived through it tell a different story, one involving cover-ups and decisions made to protect property, not people.

23
00:01:18,968 --> 00:01:20,775
So what really happened here?

24
00:01:20,775 --> 00:01:25,200
And more importantly, could it happen again, somewhere else, right now?
